discussion_comments.comment_body:
**[Suggestion]** `isSafeModeEnv()` returns an empty `disablements` Map in safe mode, but the execution-time path (`Config.getDisabledSkillNames()` via `buildDisabledSkillNamesProvider`) still enforces `skills.disabled` unconditionally. This causes a status/execution disagreement: a bundled skill listed in `skills.disabled` appears as `status: 'ok'` in the daemon `/workspace/skills` response, but invocation fails.

The deleted `readDisabledSkillNames` had no safe-mode guard and always resolved disablements. The ACP child path (`acpAgent.ts:5204-5213`) also resolves disablements unconditionally in safe mode.

Failure scenario: In safe mode, a client relying on the status API (e.g., Web Shell skill picker) shows a skill as available even though invocation fails.

```suggestion
const disablements = resolveSkillSettings(
  loadSettings(workspaceCwd, {
    consumeCorruptionEnvVars: false,
    skipLoadEnvironment: true,
  }),
).disablements;
```

