**[P2]** `setGhHost(window.host ?? undefined)` mutates the module-level `ghHost` variable in `lib/gh.ts` but is never restored.

This is a side-effect that leaks out of `auditPrWrites`. In the current flow `cleanup` runs last so nothing downstream inherits the modified host. But if any future code runs after this point (or if `auditPrWrites` is called from another context), it would inherit the Enterprise host set during audit — routing subsequent `gh` calls at the wrong host.

Consider saving and restoring the host around the audit block:

```ts
const prevHost = /* expose a getGhHost() or track locally */;
try {
  setGhHost(window.host ?? undefined);
  // ... audit work ...
} finally {
  setGhHost(prevHost);
}
```

Or scope the host override to just the `ghApiAll` calls via an option/env parameter rather than mutating shared module state.

